  "details": "<p>The archive is located near the\u00a0<span>Adad ziqqurrat in Assur.</span><span></span></p>\r\n<p><img class=\"image-inline external-image\" height=\"591\" src=\"http://oracc.ub.uni-muenchen.de/atae/images/Plan62_AssurPlan.png\" width=\"432\" /></p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Southwest of the Adad ziqqurrat in Assur, in dE5V, researchers found 6 clay tablets, some of which had envelopes, in the remains of a destroyed private house. The archive, belonging to Dadaya, dates to the reigns of A\u0161\u0161ur-etel-il\u0101ni (ca. 630\u2013627 BC) and Sin-\u0161arru-i\u0161kun (ca. 626-612 BC) and mostly contains loan documents.",
